From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:16:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] clk: rk3568: double the SD card clock the controller
 divides by two

The dw_mmc controller divides its clock input by two, which Linux and
clk_rk3399.c account for by asking the CRU for double the card rate.
clk_rk3568.c did not, so "50 MHz" High Speed ran the RG DS+ card at
25 MHz and reading the 11.75 MB kernel took 0.98 s instead of 0.50 s.

Ask the CRU for twice the rate for CLK_SDMMC0 above 1 MHz.

Upstream status: candidate (should cover the other SD/eMMC clock IDs of
the RK3568 too).
---
 drivers/clk/rockchip/clk_rk3568.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk_rk3568.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk_rk3568.c
index bb49af35..307a591e 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk_rk3568.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk_rk3568.c
@@ -1443,6 +1443,13 @@ static ulong rk3568_sdmmc_set_clk(struct rk3568_clk_priv *priv,
 	struct rk3568_cru *cru = priv->cru;
 	int src_clk;
 
+	/*
+	 * The SD controller divides its clock by two (Linux and clk_rk3399.c
+	 * ask the CRU for double), so "50 MHz" ran the card at 25 MHz.
+	 */
+	if (clk_id == CLK_SDMMC0 && rate > 1 * MHz)
+		rate *= 2;
+
 	switch (rate) {
 	case OSC_HZ:
 	case 26 * MHz:
